# The schema is the one file where a line-ending flip is genuinely dangerous: it
# turns a 25-line change into a 2,123-line diff, and a dropped hunk inside that
# is invisible on review. Pinned to LF, which is what main has always stored.
#
# Deliberately NOT applied to *.sql: the migrations are checksummed by Prisma and
# some are already applied in production, so renormalising them would rewrite
# files that must stay byte-identical to what has run.
prisma/schema.prisma text eol=lf

# المرحلة 20-4: the two generated OpenAPI artefacts, for the same reason and one
# more. They are written by `pnpm openapi:generate` and compared byte-for-byte by
# `pnpm openapi:guard`; a checkout that flipped their endings would fail the
# guard on a clean tree, on Windows only, with a diff nobody could see. Pinned to
# LF, which is what the generator writes and what CI reads.
docs/openapi.json text eol=lf
phase1-backend/src/http/openapi.document.ts text eol=lf
